        <argsstring>(model_coords, native_coords)</argsstring>
        <name>get_placement_score_from_coordinates</name>
        <qualifiedname>IMP::multifit.reference.get_placement_score_from_coordinates</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>model_coords</type>
          <defname>model_coords</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>native_coords</type>
          <defname>native_coords</defname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Computes the position error (placement distance) and the orientation error (placement angle) of the coordinates in model_coords respect to the coordinates in native_coords. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>placement distance - translation between the centroids of the coordinates placement angle - Angle in the axis-angle formulation of the rotation aligning the two rigid bodies.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>This function is only available in Python. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
